# Source Control — CLI-First Policy

All GitHub and GitLab operations (issues, PRs/MRs, projects/boards, releases) go through the official CLIs. This keeps the SDLC **tool-agnostic** — the same commands work in Claude Code, Cursor, or a plain terminal.

## Tools

- **GitHub**: `gh` CLI.
- **GitLab**: `glab` CLI.

## Which host per repo

Each project declares its repos and hosts in `.claude/stack-*.yml`. Agents read that config to determine which CLI to use per repo.

## Common operations

### GitHub (issues + boards)

```bash
# Issues
gh issue list --repo <owner>/<repo>
gh issue view <number> --repo <owner>/<repo>
gh issue create --repo <owner>/<repo> --title "..." --body "..."

# Board — read IDs from .claude/board-config.yml
gh project item-list <project_number> --owner <org> --format json
gh project item-edit \
  --project-id <project_id> \
  --id <item_id> \
  --field-id <status_field_id> \
  --single-select-option-id <status_option_id>
```

### GitLab (MRs)

```bash
glab mr list
glab mr view <number>
glab mr create --source-branch feature/<id>-<slug> \
               --target-branch <release-branch> \
               --title "<id>: <what>" \
               --description "..." \
               --remove-source-branch
glab mr merge <number>
```

## Hard rules

- **No raw API calls** (`curl` against `api.github.com` / `gitlab.com/api`) unless the CLI genuinely doesn't cover it. Prefer `gh api` / `glab api` if needed.
- **No MCP for git hosts** — CLI-based for portability across AI tools. (Client-side trackers like Jira may use MCPs — see `../../.claude/rules/F12-tracker-abstraction` once F12 lands.)
- **Never push** to `master` / `main` / `dev`. PRs/MRs target the project's declared release branch only.
- **Never open a PR/MR** from the default branch — always from `feature/<ticket-id>-<slug>` or `chore/<slug>`.
- **PR/MR title format**: `<ticket-id>: <what changed>`.
- **PR/MR body** must link the ticket and summarize the change, per `size-audit` and `agent-communication` rules.

## Pre-flight checklist for agents

Before opening any PR/MR:

- [ ] Tests green (Verification Gate passed).
- [ ] Lints clean.
- [ ] No secrets in diff (see `secrets-management`).
- [ ] Ticket is in the correct column (see `kanban-workflow`).
- [ ] PR/MR size respects `size-audit`.
